From 58d80f89e1434c211b06f6819c2a2c23b65aecd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luma <luma@simplyluma.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:19:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 72/88] arm64: luma embedded DTB: keep the bootloader's /chosen
 data

With the embedded DTB the FDT the bootloader passes in x0 was dropped, and
with it the data only the bootloader publishes under /chosen: its command
line and, on Pixel, the per-unit board id, serial number and IMEIs under
/chosen/config that the modem driver reads.

Keep that FDT's address in boot_args[0]. Early boot only reserves it, and
only when it is plain RAM clear of the kernel image and of the embedded
tree's static reserved regions. An arch_initcall then adds its bootargs as
luma,bootloader-bootargs and each /chosen subnode the embedded tree lacks to
the live tree. Embedded nodes are left untouched; values are not logged.
---
 arch/arm64/include/asm/setup.h    |   6 +
 arch/arm64/kernel/Makefile        |   2 +-
 arch/arm64/kernel/head.S          |   9 +-
 arch/arm64/kernel/luma_boot_fdt.c | 240 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm64/kernel/setup.c         |   1 +
 5 files changed, 253 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/kernel/luma_boot_fdt.c

